<title>BELGIUM: Belgian ALZ sets 4 bln Bfr CP programme.</title>
<headline>Belgian ALZ sets 4 bln Bfr CP programme.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian stainless steel maker ALZ NV and its AL-Center subsidiary, both units of Luxembourg's Arbed group, on Tuesday launched a four billion Belgian franc, multi-currency commercial paper programme.  </p>
<p>In a statement issued by lead managers Generale Bank, ALZ said the funds raised from the issue would be used to cover current operating needs.</p>
<p>Kredietbank was named as co-dealer.</p>
<p>Clearing will be through the Belgian National Bank.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
